title: Read the collator's scheduling parameters at the parent it builds on

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The slot-based collator reads `scheduling_v3_enabled`, `relay_parent_offset`,
      `max_claim_queue_offset` and the Aura authorities at the parent it builds on rather than at
      the para best head, and resolves them against `:pending_code`, so they come from the runtime
      that executes the block. This keeps candidate shape correct across a para runtime upgrade
      that flips V3 scheduling off again.

      `cumulus-pallet-parachain-system` only gains named constants for the claim queue lookahead
      and regression coverage for the `CoreInfo` `claim_queue_offset` bound; its behaviour is
      unchanged.
crates:
  - name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
    bump: patch
  - name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
    bump: patch
  - name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
    bump: patch
  - name: cumulus-primitives-core
    bump: patch
